## Block: the My turn test renders one week and taps a word from another week

`apps/storytime/__tests__/phase3-readalong-ui.test.tsx`, test "keeps My turn silent until a word tap and plays the measured word cut":

```tsx
const { audio } = await renderReader();          // default week: w01
...
const sentence = shippedTwoSentencePage().sentences[0];
const word = sentence.words[0];                  // w02 page 1: "How"
fireEvent.click(screen.getByText(new RegExp(`^${word.word...}`)));
```

`shippedTwoSentencePage()` scans the shipped weeks in folder order. The first page with two timed sentences is w02 page 1. Its sentences are "How many suns?" and "One!". Its first word is "How".

Every w01 page holds one sentence. The default reader therefore shows w01 page 1: "Hello, I am Pat.". The reader has no element with the text "How", so `getByText(/^How/)` throws. No reader implementation can pass this test.

The Red log confirms the w02 finding. The author did not see the mismatch, because the missing `reader.tsx` module stopped every app test at import time.

Fix in the Red test: pass the same source to the reader and to the word lookup:

```tsx
const { source, sentences } = shippedTwoSentencePage();
const { audio } = await renderReader(source);
const sentence = sentences[0];
```

Green checked the other Red assertions. They are implementable: the reader path and props, the audio src, the sentence text, the word cut, slow mode, the error message, the page turner, the page end, and the package ARIA and keyboard contract. The unchanged package test keeps its one sentence tab stop.

